00:49:26,666 --> 00:49:32,666
Michael David Rosenberg (born 17 May 1984), better known by his stage name
Passenger, is an English indie folk singer, songwriter and musician.

11
00:54:23,333 --> 00:54:29,333
From the 2000s, Rosenberg fronted a band by the same name; he opted to keep the
Passenger moniker for his solo work after the band dissolved.

12
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
Rosenberg is best known for the 2012 song "Let Her Go", which topped the charts in
16 countries and accumulated more than 3.9 billion views on YouTube.

13
01:04:16,666 --> 01:04:22,666
Because Rosenberg was based in Australia at the time of release (and the clip itself was filmed at the
Factory Theatre in Marrickville), it is the most-viewed Australian YouTube video ever.

14
01:09:13,333 --> 01:09:19,333
In 2014, the song was nominated for the Brit Award for British Single of the Year, and he
received the British Academy's Ivor Novello Award for Most Performed Work.

15
01:14:10,000 --> 01:14:16,000
A prolific singer-songwriter, Rosenberg has released 14 studio albums to
date: one with the band Passenger, and 13 as a solo artist.

16
01:19:06,666 --> 01:19:12,666
The most recent of these, Birds That Flew and Ships
That Sailed, was released in April 2022.

17
01:24:03,333 --> 01:24:09,333
The tone is thought_provoking.
